-- A neural (plan-enumerated) program with a constant-list arm, asked for its
-- cdf. The plan traversal tests a deterministic arm against a cumulative
-- target with planDetGuard (IRCompiler.hs), which used to emit
-- `not (val > sample)` for every non-Bool type: an OpGreaterThan on two lists,
-- always False in the interpreter (the arm counted its full mass at every
-- query) and a TypeError in Python. It now recurses structurally like
-- compareValueExpr, so a list arm takes the equality indicator.
-- x ~ N(0,1), so each arm has mass 0.5; [0.0] is <= [q] exactly for q >= 0
-- (lists are ordered componentwise), and [Normal] contributes 0.5 * Phi(q).
-- At q = 1 the list equality this used to take answered 0.5 * Phi(1) alone
-- (task head-cdf-uses-equality).
-- Task plan-det-guard-compares-composite-values-with-greater-than.
neural nn :: (Symbol -> Float)
main s = draw x = nn s in if x < 0.0 then [0.0] else [Normal]
